"{\n \"cells\": [\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"dcd1d85d\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"# Non-Hermitian SSH Lattice on 4N+1 Sites\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"**Interactive Python port** of the MATLAB simulation built while writing\\n\",\n    \"*Xu et al., \\\"Electrical circuit simulation of non-Hermitian lattice models\\\"*,\\n\",\n    \"Acta Phys. Sin. 72, 200301 (2023) — a first-author **review** of classical-circuit\\n\",\n    \"emulation of non-Hermitian lattice models.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"The code here is an **independent implementation** for understanding the physics\\n\",\n    \"surveyed in the review: it is not part of the article itself.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"## Physics in one paragraph\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"The optics–quantum analogy maps paraxial light propagation in waveguide arrays\\n\",\n    \"onto the Schrödinger equation, so a chain of coupled waveguides emulates a\\n\",\n    \"tight-binding model. The **SSH chain** (staggered hoppings $J_1, J_2$) is the\\n\",\n    \"canonical topological lattice. Adding **gain/loss** $\\\\pm i\\\\gamma$ makes the\\n\",\n    \"Hamiltonian non-Hermitian:\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"- complex eigenvalues appear when $\\\\gamma$ exceeds the **PT-symmetry breaking** threshold;\\n\",\n    \"- eigenstates localize (large **IPR** — inverse participation ratio) at a boundary.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"The 4N+1-site construction studied here connects two SSH halves through a central\\n\",\n    \"site $b_N$, with variants controlling the gain/loss phase pattern.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"Let's explore it numerically.\\n\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"cf62af11\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"# setup\\n\",\n    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n    \"from ssh_lattice import build_hamiltonian, spectrum, time_evolve, demo_defaults\\n\",\n    \"%matplotlib inline\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"03ebf105\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## 1. Build the Hamiltonian\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"The 4N+1-site chain: site $a_0$ (gain $+i\\\\gamma$), first half (n=1..N, intra $J_1$/inter $J_2$),\\n\",\n    \"connecting site $b_N$, second half (n=N+1..2N, intra $J_2$/inter $J_1$).\\n\",\n    \"Variant `a`: same-phase PT pattern; `b`: anti-phase; `c`: anti-phase with $b_N$ gaining.\\n\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"a468d41e\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"N, gamma, J1, J2 = 10, 0.0, 0.5, 1.5\\n\",\n    \"H = build_hamiltonian(N, gamma, J1, J2, variant='a')\\n\",\n    \"print('dimension:', H.shape, ' (4N+1 =', 4*N+1, ')')\\n\",\n    \"print('first 6 rows of the sparse pattern:')\\n\",\n    \"print(H[:6, :6])\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"892510f8\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## 2. Spectrum & PT breaking\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"With $\\\\gamma=0$ the Hamiltonian is Hermitian — all eigenvalues real.\\n\",\n    \"As $\\\\gamma$ grows, complex pairs appear: this is the **PT-symmetry breaking transition**.\\n\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"5cde9a58\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"eigvals, _ = spectrum(H)\\n\",\n    \"plt.figure(figsize=(8,4))\\n\",\n    \"plt.plot(np.arange(1, 4*N+2), eigvals.real, 'b.', ms=12)\\n\",\n    \"plt.xlabel('Eigenstate index'); plt.ylabel(r'Re $E$')\\n\",\n    \"plt.title(f'Spectrum at $\\\\gamma$={gamma} (Hermitian limit)')\\n\",\n    \"plt.grid(alpha=0.3); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"a49e5b3f\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"# sweep gamma -> complex spectrum\\n\",\n    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(14, 4))\\n\",\n    \"for ax, g in zip(axes, [0.5, 1.5, 3.0]):\\n\",\n    \"    ev, _ = spectrum(build_hamiltonian(N, g, J1, J2, 'a'))\\n\",\n    \"    ax.plot(ev.real, ev.imag, 'o', ms=5, mfc='none', mec='C0')\\n\",\n    \"    ax.axhline(0, color='k', lw=0.6)\\n\",\n    \"    ax.set_title(rf'$\\\\gamma$={g}')\\n\",\n    \"    ax.set_xlabel(r'Re $E$'); ax.set_ylabel(r'Im $E$')\\n\",\n    \"    ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n    \"fig.suptitle('PT-symmetry breaking: complex eigenvalues appear'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"800217df\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## 3. Time evolution from $b_N$\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"Initialize the state on the central site $b_N$ and evolve with $U = e^{-iH\\\\Delta t}$.\\n\",\n    \"Track the probability on $b_N$ and the **IPR** (localization measure).\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"$$\\\\mathrm{IPR}(t) = \\\\frac{\\\\sum_i |\\\\psi_i|^4}{(\\\\sum_i |\\\\psi_i|^2)^2}$$\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"High IPR = localized state.\\n\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"aeb64699\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"psi0 = np.zeros(4*N+1, dtype=complex)\\n\",\n    \"bN = 2*N                       # central site (0-based)\\n\",\n    \"psi0[bN] = 1.0\\n\",\n    \"t, psi_t, prob_bN, ipr = time_evolve(H, psi0, t_max=1.0, dt=0.01, target_index=bN)\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\\n\",\n    \"ax1.plot(t, prob_bN, lw=2)\\n\",\n    \"ax1.set_xlabel('Time'); ax1.set_ylabel(r'$|\\\\psi(b_N)|^2$')\\n\",\n    \"ax1.set_title('Probability on the central site'); ax1.grid(alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n    \"ax2.plot(t, ipr, lw=2, color='tab:red')\\n\",\n    \"ax2.set_xlabel('Time'); ax2.set_ylabel('IPR')\\n\",\n    \"ax2.set_title('Inverse participation ratio'); ax2.grid(alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n    \"plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"4b97968d\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"# density heatmap\\n\",\n    \"prob = np.abs(psi_t)**2\\n\",\n    \"plt.figure(figsize=(9, 4))\\n\",\n    \"plt.imshow(prob.T, aspect='auto', origin='lower', extent=[0, 4*N+1, 0, 1.0], cmap='magma')\\n\",\n    \"plt.xlabel('Lattice site'); plt.ylabel('Time')\\n\",\n    \"plt.title('Probability density evolution from b_N')\\n\",\n    \"plt.colorbar(label='probability'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"10ccc9dd\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## 4. Variant comparison at finite gain/loss\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"At $\\\\gamma=2.5$, the three variants develop different complex spectra and\\n\",\n    \"localization behavior. Run `compare_variants.py` for the full comparison, or:\\n\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n   \"execution_count\": null,\n   \"id\": \"0c02250f\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"outputs\": [],\n   \"source\": [\n    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4), sharey=True)\\n\",\n    \"for ax, v in zip(axes, 'abc'):\\n\",\n    \"    p = demo_defaults('c' if v=='c' else 'a')\\n\",\n    \"    Hv = build_hamiltonian(p['N'], p['gamma'], p['J1'], p['J2'], v)\\n\",\n    \"    psi = np.zeros(4*p['N']+1, dtype=complex); psi[2*p['N']] = 1.0\\n\",\n    \"    _, pt, _, _ = time_evolve(Hv, psi, p['t_max'], p['dt'], 2*p['N'])\\n\",\n    \"    fp = np.abs(pt[:,-1])**2\\n\",\n    \"    ax.bar(np.arange(1, len(fp)+1), fp, width=1)\\n\",\n    \"    ax.set_title(f'variant {v} (N={p[\\\"N\\\"]}, $\\\\\\\\gamma$={p[\\\"gamma\\\"]})')\\n\",\n    \"    ax.set_xlabel('Lattice site'); ax.grid(alpha=0.3, axis='y')\\n\",\n    \"axes[0].set_ylabel('Final probability')\\n\",\n    \"fig.suptitle('Final-state distributions: same initial state, three variants')\\n\",\n    \"plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"8ffdc940\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"## Next steps\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"- The 4N+1 geometry is a playground for studying PT symmetry, skin effect and\\n\",\n    \"  non-Hermitian topology — try scanning $\\\\gamma$ and watching the zero modes.\\n\",\n    \"- A data-driven extension: learn the *dynamics* with a Neural ODE — see the\\n\",\n    \"  [Neural ODE double-pendulum project](https://github.com/sj-nosugar/neutral-ode-double-pendulum)\\n\",\n    \"  for the physics → data → learned dynamics → control pipeline.\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"*All figures in this repository use English labels.*\\n\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"metadata\": {\n  \"kernelspec\": {\n   \"display_name\": \"Python 3\",\n   \"language\": \"python\",\n   \"name\": \"python3\"\n  }\n },\n \"nbformat\": 4,\n \"nbformat_minor\": 5\n}"